1
00:00:00,470 --> 00:00:04,730
Thirty students, one class
timeline, and nobody can wreck it.

2
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:05,790
Here's how.

3
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:10,630
Add your students as contributors.
Their changes don't go straight in:

4
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:14,776
each one becomes a proposal, showing
exactly what it adds and changes.

5
00:00:15,046 --> 00:00:18,226
You talk it through, then
merge it or reject it.

6
00:00:18,276 --> 00:00:21,932
Every save is kept in the history,
so you can always go back.

7
00:00:22,262 --> 00:00:24,802
Make it public, and anyone
can read it with one link,

8
00:00:24,852 --> 00:00:29,125
no account needed. Students
can even fork their own copy.

9
00:00:29,215 --> 00:00:31,757
It's OpenChronology, and it's free.
